{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"Foundation Medicine's tissue CGP code 0037U lost about 11% of Medicare volume in 2024 at a flat CMS price, and its liquid code 0239U was flat.","detail":"National Medicare Part B services for 0037U (FoundationOne CDx tissue) fell from 15,551 (15,460 beneficiaries) to 13,787 (13,693 beneficiaries), which is −11.3%. The average allowed payment was $3,421 vs $3,418, so the price did not move. The liquid code 0239U was 7,188 vs 7,181 services (−0.1%) at $3,424 vs $3,423. Comprehensive genomic profiling (CGP, large cancer gene panels), one of Illumina's biggest clinical Gb pools, is therefore flat to shrinking in the Medicare fee-for-service base. The two releases are the two 'by Geography and Service' datasets I queried. I labelled them 2023 (ddee9e22…) and 2024 (6fea9d79…) because the 0340U figures match known 2024 facts: +87% services and −8.3% payment. The year labels are inferred, not read from a field.","url":"https://data.cms.gov/data-api/v1/dataset/6fea9d79-0129-4e4c-b1b8-23cd86a4f435/data?filter[Rndrng_Prvdr_Geo_Lvl]=National&filter[HCPCS_Cd]=0037U","date":"2026 release (CY2024 data, inferred)","source_name":"CMS Medicare Physician & Other Practitioners by Geography and Service (data.cms.gov API)","source_type":"claims_data","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Code-level 0037U and 0239U volume and price are not in the known list. F430 and F674 give only an aggregate FMI figure and a three-customer summary."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"Guardant360 liquid volume in Medicare grew only about 4% across its two main codes, 0242U and 0326U, even though dollars grew about 19%.","detail":"The 0242U code (Guardant360 CDx) went from 21,416 to 20,206 services (−5.6%) at a flat ~$4,890. The 0326U code (the liquid LDT code) went from 16,798 to 19,695 (+17.3%), with payment rising from $3,533 to $4,892. Combined services were 38,214 → 39,901, which is +4.4%. Combined dollars were about $164.1M → $195.2M (+19%), computed from services × average payment. So dollar growth comes from the 0326U rate reset, not from more tests. The 0334U tissue code did grow, from 1,941 to 2,759 services (+42%), but at $3,075 it is a small line of about $8.5M.","url":"https://data.cms.gov/data-api/v1/dataset/92396110-2aed-4d63-a6a2-5d6207d46a29/data?filter[Rndrng_Prvdr_Last_Org_Name]=Guardant Health, Inc.","date":"2026 release (CY2024 data, inferred)","source_name":"CMS Medicare Physician & Other Practitioners by Provider and Service (data.cms.gov API)","source_type":"claims_data","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"This adds the combined 0242U+0326U volume (+4.4%) and the dollar arithmetic. D038 and F429 covered only 0326U or called volume 'flat'."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"Medicare whole-genome volume is tiny: 131 genome claims nationally in 2024, 127 of them from Baylor.","detail":"Code 81425 (genome sequencing) had 131 national services in 2024 (127 from Baylor Miraca Genetics) at $4,931 each. That is roughly 15,700 Gb at an assumed 120 Gb per genome, or about 0.002% of a ~800M Gb high-throughput base. Counts under 11 are suppressed, so the true total is slightly higher. The 2023 national figure was 13, so growth was ~10x, but from a negligible base. WGS is therefore growing fast but is nowhere near enough to offset slower NIPT or CGP volume in Medicare. This is Medicare fee-for-service only, so commercial rapid-WGS volume is not captured.","url":"https://data.cms.gov/data-api/v1/dataset/92396110-2aed-4d63-a6a2-5d6207d46a29/data?filter[c][condition][path]=HCPCS_Cd&filter[c][condition][operator]=IN&filter[c][condition][value][]=81425","date":"2026 release (CY2024 data, inferred)","source_name":"CMS Medicare Physician & Other Practitioners (data.cms.gov API)","source_type":"claims_data","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"This quantifies WGS in Gb terms, with the 13 → 131 change. F720 and F676 say only 'negligible'."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"supports","claim":"The Medicare beneficiary count for Natera's Signatera MRD code is about 51 times that of the one Guardant MRD-like code, whose identity I did not confirm.","detail":"Natera 0340U had 11,922 beneficiaries and 25,746 services. Guardant 0422U ('Onc pan solid tum alys DNA') had 232 beneficiaries and 243 services at $1,897. I did not confirm that 0422U is Guardant Reveal, so treat that as unverified. MRD Medicare volume is concentrated in one vendor. Outside Natera, MRD is still tiny, which supports the claim that MRD is not yet a broad Gb pool.","url":"https://data.cms.gov/data-api/v1/dataset/92396110-2aed-4d63-a6a2-5d6207d46a29/data?filter[Rndrng_Prvdr_Last_Org_Name]=Guardant Health, Inc.","date":"2026 release (CY2024 data, inferred)","source_name":"CMS Medicare Physician & Other Practitioners (data.cms.gov API)","source_type":"claims_data","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The competitor MRD code magnitude and the concentration ratio are not in the known list."},
{"label":"1C","direction":"against","claim":"Some Medicare code counts moved sharply, which may mean volume growth is hidden by coding shifts. The 'against' reading is ambiguous.","detail":"81455 (51+ gene panel) fell from 41,582 to 13,895 services, while 81419 (epilepsy panel) rose from 6,072 to 30,385. Adaptive's 81479 line holds 5,123 services at $7,099. These swings look like billing or coding migration between codes, not real volume change. Code-level Medicare series are therefore unreliable for per-test trends unless the codes are tied to a lab. I did not verify the cause.","url":"https://data.cms.gov/data-api/v1/dataset/6fea9d79-0129-4e4c-b1b8-23cd86a4f435/data?filter[Rndrng_Prvdr_Geo_Lvl]=National&filter[HCPCS_Cd]=81455","date":"2026 release","source_name":"CMS Medicare Physician & Other Practitioners (data.cms.gov API)","source_type":"claims_data","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"This is a data-quality caveat for the Medicare claims reads used so far, with the specific code swings quantified."}
